tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-252-a-library-name-no-windows-linker-reads-as-one-file.hero:31:23: error[unwritable_name]: this library's name holds `/`, which every linker reads as a directory and not the same one, `sub/m.lib` on Windows and `libsub/m` on macOS and Linux, so `sub/m` does not name one file on every machine: write the name without it, as `link "m"`
