tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-252-a-library-name-no-windows-linker-reads-as-one-file.hero:49:23: error[unwritable_name]: this library's name holds `\`, which no file's name on Windows can hold, and `C:\\side\\m` names a path from a root, where this machine keeps the library rather than what the machine has
  pass `--library <dir>` with the directory holding it, or name a `package` and let `pkg-config` answer; `link` takes the library's **name**, as `link "sqlite3"`
